89
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.990
Hi, Dr. Hamilton, how are you?

90
00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.220
I'm great, so happy to be here.

91
00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.970
Us too,

92
00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:29.330
and I think that Alicia's case

93
00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:33.010
is sounding very specific, and I think we can attack it.

94
00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.620
What are the biggest causes of not being able to sleep?

95
00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.180
Yeah, you know, there are a number of things

96
00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.230 line:15%
that control our sleep, and sometimes it can be

97
00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.860 line:15%
something insignificant or temporary,

98
00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.610 line:15%
or a lifestyle change, that can affect our sleep

99
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.220 line:15%
and cause a chronic, persistent problem.

100
00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.250
So, Alicia mentioned she works the double shift,

101
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.790
so now her schedule is all over the place,

102
00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.200
and that's really important.

103
00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.330
Our sleep is controlled by our circadian rhythm

104
00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.964
or our internal clock, and it likes consistency.

105
00:04:01.964 --> 00:04:05.040
So, it's important to have those consistent bedtimes

106
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.410
if you can.

107
00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.500
A lot of people have Sunday night insomnia.

108
00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.790
That's when you sleep in on your days off

109
00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.450
or you nap all weekend long,

110
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.010
and then when Sunday night comes,

111
00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.090
you've now set the stage for difficulty falling asleep

112
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.420
for the rest of the week.

113
00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.760
Okay, so for the past week, Dr. Hamilton performed

114
00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.400
a sleep experiment with Alicia

115
00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.930 line:15%
to help her examine her sleep patterns.

116
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.290 line:15%
Dr. Hamilton, what did you find?

117
00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.620 line:15%
So, a couple of things.

118
00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.510
For one thing, she went into REM sleep pretty quickly,

119
00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.650
which suggests either sleep deprivation

120
00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:36.970
or other sleep issues.

121
00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.210
You also had less REM sleep, Alicia.

122
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.040
You were at about maybe 16%,

123
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:45.000
when normal REM sleep is 20 to 25%,

124
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.920
and REM sleep is very important.

125
00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.360
That's our most restorative stage of sleep,

126
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.880
so it's really important to get that REM sleep.

127
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.930
What does she do?

128
00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.630 line:15%
The first thing to do is to prioritize your sleep.

129
00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.180 line:15%
You know, everyone sets a morning alarm

130
00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.880 line:15%
so you're not late to work or that important meeting.

131
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.310
I would set a bedtime alarm and, of course,

132
00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:04.930
shutting off the screens.
Yes.

133
00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.150
Shutting off the TV, shutting off the phone.

134
00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.030
You know, when you watch something at night,

135
00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.040
you get lost in it, or you end up,

136
00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.530
if you start scrolling, you get stuck scrolling forever.

137
00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.620
So, it distracts you, and the other important thing

138
00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.010
is the blue wavelengths,

139
00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.300
those blue lights emitted from the screens,

140
00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.510
prevent your natural melatonin from being secreted.

141
00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.600
Alicia, do you have blue light glasses?

142
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.940
No.
I make some

143
00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:30.950
